Dear colleagues,

Following a review of how staff accounts are protected, three changes
are being made. They apply to every member of staff at all four
campuses, including part-time and visiting staff.

1. Multi-factor authentication becomes compulsory

Every staff account must be enrolled in multi-factor authentication
(MFA) by Saturday 31 January 2026. Once enrolled, you will be asked to
confirm each sign-in from a new device with the HIT Verify app or with
a hardware key. On a device you have already confirmed, you will be
asked again every 30 days.

Any account that has not been enrolled will be suspended on Monday
2 February 2026 on the instruction of the Chief Information Security
Officer. A suspended account can be restored only in person at the
help desk, with your staff badge.

At the moment 212 of our 540 staff accounts are enrolled, so most of
you still need to act. Enrolment takes about five minutes at
https://verify.halvorsen-institute.example.

Staff who do not have a smartphone can collect a hardware key free of
charge from the help desk. A lost key costs $25 to replace.

2. Passwords

From 5 January 2026 a password must be at least 14 characters long.
The old rule of 10 characters is withdrawn. In return, you will be
asked to change your password once every 365 days instead of every 90
days. You will be prompted to choose a new password the first time you
sign in after 5 January.

Please do not reuse a password that you use anywhere else, and never
type it into a page you reached from a link in an e-mail. The help desk
will never ask you for your password.

3. Laptop replacement

Staff laptops that are more than five years old will be replaced
between February and May 2026. There are 138 such devices. You will be
contacted by the help desk to arrange a time; you do not need to do
anything now. Devices are replaced in order of age, oldest first.

Getting help

The help desk is in the Vasterling Building, room 0.09, and is open on
weekdays from 08:00 to 18:00. You can call extension 4100 or write to
helpdesk@halvorsen-institute.example.

We are also running drop-in MFA clinics in the Thistlewood Library,
room L-2, on 10, 12 and 17 December from 12:00 to 14:00. Colleagues at
Toronto, Lisbon and Pune will receive separate invitations from their
local IT teams.

Thank you for your co-operation.

Leonie Brandvold
Director of IT Services
Halvorsen Institute of Technology
